# Copy this file to .env in the project root and adjust values.
# See utils/config.py for the full list of supported variables and their defaults.
#
# Paths below (MODEL_PATH, DB_PATH, RAG_DATA_DIR, INDEX_PATH, META_PATH) may be
# relative or absolute. A relative path is resolved against the project root
# (the directory containing app.py), not against whatever directory you
# happen to launch the app from — so it stays correct however you start it
# (interactively, via a different shell, or via the systemd unit).

HOST=0.0.0.0
PORT=4010

MODEL_PATH=models/Qwen3.5-9B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
# Download: https://huggingface.co/unsloth/Qwen3.5-9B-GGUF/resolve/main/Qwen3.5-9B-UD-Q4_K_XL.gguf
# Replaced the earlier Qwen2.5-3B-instruct reference model after real
# testing on the same (weak, CPU-only) reference hardware: noticeably
# fewer of the small model's characteristic failures (contradicting a
# tool's own computed verdict, inventing facts not in the data, garbling
# non-Russian text) at a real but tolerable cost in latency (a full
# RAG-interpreted horary answer ran 400-550s on the reference i7-5500U,
# vs ~250s for the 3B model — see utils/config.py's REPEAT_PENALTY comment
# and utils/llm.py's <think>-block stripping, both written with this
# model's "-Thinking-" heritage in mind). unsloth/Qwen3.5-9B-GGUF also
# ships plain (non-"UD") K-quants (e.g. Qwen3.5-9B-Q4_K_M.gguf) if this
# dynamic quant ever fails to load on an older llama-cpp-python build —
# swap the filename above and below, nothing else needs to change. Ignore
# the mmproj-*.gguf files in that repo entirely — those are for the
# model's image-understanding half, unused here (this app only calls
# create_chat_completion for text).

# Uncomment to override LLM inference defaults:
# N_THREADS=4    # token-GENERATION threads only. Counterintuitive real-world result on a
# 6-core/12-thread i7-8700: 4 measured faster end-to-end than both 6 and 10 on the same
# prompt — generation is memory-bandwidth-bound with a per-token sync barrier across
# threads, so more threads can add more overhead than parallelism past a point that
# depends on your memory bandwidth, not your core count. Re-measure a real request
# end-to-end before trusting a higher number here — don't assume it from core count alone.
# N_THREADS_BATCH=12  # prompt-processing threads — a SEPARATE setting from N_THREADS above,
# for the more parallelizable prefill phase. Previously not set anywhere in this project,
# which meant llama-cpp-python silently used every logical core for this phase regardless
# of N_THREADS — that's why every CPU could show ~100% even with N_THREADS turned down.
# Defaults to your full logical core count if left unset (unchanged prior behavior).
# N_BATCH=512    # prompt tokens processed per batch (a size, not a thread count) during
# prefill. Real test: N_THREADS_BATCH=8 + N_BATCH=2048 together measured WORSE end-to-end
# (31 min) than leaving both at these plain defaults (835s, same technique) — the tool/data
# steps were fast in that run, the slowdown was in generation itself. Leave both unset
# unless you test a change with several repeated runs of the SAME query, not a one-off
# comparison across different requests — see README's "Tuning CPU inference threads".
# N_CTX=32768   # plenty of headroom below this model's own native window (262144, extensible far beyond that) — raise only if you actually need longer prompts and can spare the RAM
# N_GPU_LAYERS=0
# REPEAT_PENALTY=1.15  # raise if the model starts glitching into repeated/foreign-script text on long answers

# Uncomment to override chat history storage:
# DB_PATH=data/chat.sqlite3

# RAG (optional) — uncomment to override:
# RAG_DATA_DIR=rag_data
# INDEX_DIR=data/rag_index      # one faiss_index.bin+meta.pkl per corpus lives under here (build_index.py)
# INDEX_PATH=data/faiss_index.bin  # legacy single-index fallback only — see utils/rag.py
# META_PATH=data/meta.pkl          # legacy single-index fallback only — see utils/rag.py
# INDEX_CONCURRENCY=4          # concurrent external processes (tesseract, antiword, ...) while indexing
# EMBED_MODEL=paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2
# TOP_K=3
# RAG_ALWAYS_INCLUDE_MAX_CHARS=28000  # raised from 16000: both horary_methodology.txt (~20400 chars)
# and the astro_progressions bundle (~18300 chars combined) grew past the old cap, which was
# silently dropping their tail sections (symbol legend, answer structure, worked example) — see
# utils/config.py's own comment for the full story and how to re-check this for your own corpus.

# Rectification tools (astro_rectification_trutine / astro_rectification_events):
# off by default — these return the tool's own computed report directly,
# with no follow-up LLM call at all. Real testing with the ORIGINAL
# Qwen2.5-3B reference model showed the follow-up call reliably
# contradicting the tool's own computed best-candidate time in its own
# prose, even after several rounds of prompt-level mitigation (see
# utils/config.py's own comment on this setting for the full story). A
# noticeably more capable model is now the default above (Qwen3.5-9B) —
# worth re-testing this toggle against it, but it hasn't been re-verified
# yet as of this writing, so it stays off here until that's actually been
# done, not just assumed from the model swap alone.
# RECTIFICATION_LLM_FOLLOWUP=false

# Hugging Face Hub access (used by the RAG embedding model and, if
# installed, CLIPSeg on ycplt_img). "Warning: You are sending
# unauthenticated requests..." on every startup is expected and harmless —
# SentenceTransformer(...) pings the Hub on every load to check the cache
# is current, even once the model is already downloaded, unless told not
# to. Two independent ways to quiet it, pick either (or neither, it's just
# a warning):
#   - HF_TOKEN: a free account token (https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens)
#     raises the rate limit and silences the "unauthenticated" warning, but
#     still makes a network call every startup.
#   - HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1: once the model is already cached locally (after the
#     first successful startup/build_index.py run), this skips the network
#     check entirely — faster startup, works with no internet at all, and
#     matches this project's local-first design better than a token does.
#     Don't set it before the very first run, though: the model has to be
#     downloaded once with network access before "offline" makes sense.
# HF_TOKEN=
HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1

# Image generation service (ycplt_img, on a separate machine):
IMAGE_SERVICE_HOST=192.168.7.7
IMAGE_SERVICE_PORT=4011
# IMAGE_POLL_INTERVAL_SEC=10
# IMAGE_HTTP_TIMEOUT_SEC=10

# Note: no vision/captioning model settings here — this app only hosts the
# chat LLM. Image understanding is handled by ycplt_img (mode="caption");
# see that project's own .env.example for VISION_MODEL/VISION_MMPROJ.
